---
import Account from "../layouts/Account.astro";
import PublisherJourney from "../components/PublisherJourney.astro";
import { extensionMarkPath, extensionMarkViewBox } from "../lib/extensionMark";
import "../styles/publish-studio.css";
---
<Account title="Your next" titleAccent="release" section="publish">
  <div class="publish-studio">
    <PublisherJourney current="package" />
    <section class="publish-gate" aria-labelledby="publish-gate-title"><span class="publish-gate-mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><h2 id="publish-gate-title">Checking submission availability…</h2><p id="publish-availability-note" role="status">Your preparation stays separate from sending a package.</p></div><a href="/docs/extensions/publishing" class="quiet-text-link">How publishing works ↗</a></section>
    <div class="publish-studio-layout">
      <form id="publish-form" class="publish-studio-form" novalidate>
        <fieldset id="publish-fields" disabled>
          <legend class="sr-only">Prepare your extension</legend>
          <section class="release-form-step" aria-labelledby="publish-identity-heading"><div class="release-step-heading"><span class="release-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h2 id="publish-identity-heading">Who’s it from?</h2><p>Your namespace is the publisher name on this release.</p></div></div>
            <label for="publish-namespace">Publisher namespace</label><select id="publish-namespace" required aria-describedby="publish-namespace-help"><option value="">Choose your publisher name</option></select><p class="field-help" id="publish-namespace-help">Loading your namespaces…</p><a class="quiet-text-link" href="/account/namespaces">Manage publisher names ↗</a>
            <details class="publish-name-planner"><summary id="name-planner-heading">Naming a new extension?</summary><div><p>Already built your package? Its name comes from the archive. Use this optional planner when you’re still choosing a name.</p><div class="name-planner-fields"><div><label for="tool-display-name">Display name</label><input id="tool-display-name" maxlength="100" placeholder="My lovely tool" /></div><div><label for="tool-package-name">Package name</label><input id="tool-package-name" maxlength="63" placeholder="my-tool" aria-describedby="tool-name-status" /></div></div><div class="name-planner-actions"><button type="button" id="tool-name-check" class="button secondary">Check package name</button><a id="tool-name-search" href="/extensions">Explore similar tools ↗</a></div><p id="tool-name-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a namespace and enter a package name to check it.</p><div id="tool-name-selection" hidden><p><strong id="tool-name-title"></strong><br /><code id="tool-name-id"></code></p><p>Use these values in <code>tabs-extension.json</code> before building. Checking a name does not reserve it or rename an archive.</p><pre id="tool-name-manifest"></pre><button id="tool-name-copy" type="button" class="button secondary">Copy manifest fields</button></div><details class="extension-naming-help"><summary>Can two tools share a name?</summary><p>Display names can be shared. Each package name identifies one tool within its publisher namespace. Use that same identity when releasing a new version.</p></details></div></details>
          </section>
          <section class="release-form-step" aria-labelledby="publish-package-heading"><div class="release-step-heading"><span class="release-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h2 id="publish-package-heading">Bring your package.</h2><p>Selecting a file stays on your device. Nothing is uploaded yet.</p></div></div>
            <div id="publish-drop" class="studio-package-drop"><span class="studio-drop-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox={extensionMarkViewBox} fill="currentColor"><path d={extensionMarkPath} fill-rule="evenodd" /></svg></span><h3>Drop a little possibility here.</h3><p>One built <code>.tabsext</code> archive.</p><input id="publish-file" tabindex="-1" hidden type="file" accept=".tabsext" aria-label="Choose a package" aria-describedby="publish-file-help" required /><button type="button" class="button secondary" id="publish-choose-file" aria-describedby="publish-file-help">Choose a package ↗</button><p id="publish-file-help" class="field-help">Up to 25 MiB compressed · 50 MiB unpacked.</p></div>
            <div class="studio-file-selection"><p id="publish-file-summary" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="button" id="publish-remove-file" class="quiet-remove" hidden>Remove file</button></div><p id="publish-status" class="studio-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking your publishing account…</p>
            <details class="package-size-help"><summary>What if my extension is bigger?</summary><p>The current limit is 25 MiB for the uploaded archive and 50 MiB after unpacking. Include only the files your tool needs to run, rather than development dependencies, caches, or build tooling.</p><p>Larger archives, including multi-gigabyte packages, aren’t supported yet. Supporting them needs changes to packaging, upload, review, and installation—not just a larger file picker limit.</p></details>
          </section>
          <section class="release-form-step release-submit-step" aria-labelledby="publish-send-heading"><div class="release-step-heading"><span class="release-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h2 id="publish-send-heading">Ready when you are.</h2><p>Sending starts the review process. It doesn’t publish instantly.</p></div></div>
            <div id="publish-agreement-panel"><label class="publisher-agreement"><input id="publish-agreement" type="checkbox" required /><span>I have read and accept the <a href="/publisher-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">publisher terms<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</span></label><p id="publish-terms" class="field-help">Loading the current terms…</p></div>
            <p id="publish-submit-note" class="release-submit-note">Checking what’s needed before you can send.</p><button class="button" type="submit" disabled>Submit for review ↗</button><progress id="publish-progress" max="100" value="0" aria-label="Package upload progress" hidden></progress><button id="publish-cancel" class="button secondary" type="button" hidden>Cancel upload</button>
          </section>
        </fieldset>
      </form>
      <aside class="release-sidecar" aria-label="Your package preparation"><section class="release-receipt"><div class="release-parcel" aria-hidden="true"><span class="parcel-caption">YOUR IDEA, ALL WRAPPED UP</span><div class="release-parcel-sheet"><span>FROM YOUR WORKSPACE</span><svg viewBox={extensionMarkViewBox} fill="currentColor"><path d={extensionMarkPath} fill-rule="evenodd" /></svg><strong>something-good.tabsext</strong><i>↗</i></div><div class="release-parcel-route"><span>You</span><span>······ ↗ ······</span><span>A new workspace</span></div></div><span class="desk-kicker">YOUR RELEASE, AT A GLANCE</span><div class="release-receipt-heading"><span class="receipt-spark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><h2>A good idea,<br /><em class="editorial-accent">taking shape.</em></h2></div><dl><div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd id="publish-summary-namespace">Choose a namespace</dd></div><div><dt>Package</dt><dd id="publish-summary-package">No file selected</dd></div><div><dt>Submission</dt><dd id="publish-summary-availability">Checking availability</dd></div></dl><p id="publish-local-check-note">File selection checks the extension and archive size. Package contents and publisher identity are validated by the registry after upload.</p></section><section class="release-aftercare"><span class="desk-kicker">AFTER YOU SEND</span><ol><li><strong>Package checks</strong><p>The registry validates and scans the archive.</p></li><li><strong>A human review</strong><p>Follow progress and feedback in Submissions.</p></li><li><strong>A signed release</strong><p>Approved versions become available after signed publication.</p></li></ol><a href="/account/extensions" class="quiet-text-link">Your submissions ↗</a></section><a class="release-builder-link" href="/developers"><strong>Still putting it together?</strong><span>Open the developer toolkit ↗</span></a></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Account>
<script>
  import "../scripts/publish";
  import "../scripts/tool-naming";
</script>
